{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/PreDefinition/EqUnfold.html#Lean.Meta.getConstUnfoldEqnFor?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">getConstUnfoldEqnFor?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">declName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the \"const unfold\" theorem (`f.eq_unfold`) for the given declaration.\nThis is not extensible, and always builds on the unfold theorem (`f.eq_def`).","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/PreDefinition/EqUnfold.html#Lean.Meta.getConstUnfoldEqnFor?","kind":"def","line":18,"name":"Lean.Meta.getConstUnfoldEqnFor?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Elab/PreDefinition/EqUnfold.lean#L18-L55"}}],"imports":["Lean.Elab.PreDefinition.EqnsUtils","Lean.Meta.Eqns","Lean.Meta.Tactic.Intro","Lean.Meta.Tactic.Rfl"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Elab.PreDefinition.EqUnfold"}